// Input: what the pointer and the keyboard did this frame.
//
// Three drags share one piece of state (ed_st slot 5) because only one can be
// happening: the button that started it owns it until it comes up. See drag.id
// for which button means what.

// sys_sync first: the surface is the window, and its size has to be settled
// before a single rect is laid out. Doing it here rather than at present time is
// what keeps a resize from shearing the frame it happened in.
ed_input() {
  sys_sync();
  ed_input2();
} return void;

ed_input2() {
  int drain_v = inp_drain();
  run_quit(drain_v);
  ed_orbit();
} return void;
